DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaccppiissuurrffaaccee driver provides ACPI support for Microsoft Surface Book
     laptops.  It responds to various button presses such as volume up/down
     and power buttons, all of which are located on the top of the tablet/de‐
     tachable display.  It does not provide support for the hotkeys in the
     keyboard/base unit.

     Volume up/down button presses are routed to the master system mixer via
     the wscons(4) subsystem.  Power button presses result in a soft power off
     request being queued by the acpi(4) subsystem.

